WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.601
-Good evening, everybody.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.601
This is "Late Night."
How is everybody doing tonight?

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
Great to hear.

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:09.467
In that case,
let's get to the news.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:12.968
President Biden spoke on Monday
from his coronavirus quarantine

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:15.734
to announce that the U.S.
had killed Al Qaeda leader

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.400
Ayman al-Zawahiri,

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.133
which kind of sets
unreasonable expectations

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:22.501
about how much work
we're supposed to get done

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:24.734
while having COVID.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:28.367
You ordered the killing of
Al Qaeda's top guy with COVID.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:32.601
I didn't even tell jokes
about it while I had COVID.

00:00:32.601 --> 00:00:35.234
According to a new report,
U.S. intelligence officials

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.901
killed Al Qaeda leader
Ayman al-Zawahiri

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.200
after tracking him down
through his family.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.968
Yet another reason not to accept
a Facebook friend request

00:00:43.968 --> 00:00:45.968
from your aunt.

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:47.934
"Is that a drone?

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:49.734
Peggy!"

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:54.033
First Lady Dr. Jill Biden
said in a new interview

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:56.300
that she has dinner
with President Biden most nights

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.968
and they turn off the television
to spend time together.

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.934
Also, nothing good's on
at 4:00 p.m.

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:04.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.667
The First Lady also said that,
despite her busy schedule,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.434
she gets 7 1/2 hours
of sleep most nights.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:14.501
Apparently, her secret is asking
Joe to tell her about his day.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.734
"You're not going to
believe this part."

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:20.067
"Mm-hmm."

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.501
Ahead of Missouri's
Republican Senate primary,

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.267
former President Trump on Monday

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:27.634
posted to his Truth Social
platform

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:30.067
that he was endorsing Eric
but did not mention

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.300
whether it was former
Governor Eric Greitens

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.367
or State Attorney General
Eric Schmitt.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:37.367
Said Trump, "Neither. Menendez."

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.601
It's not too soon, is it?

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.834
Oh, just too bad?

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.033
Just keep him up
a second longer.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:56.434
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.400
departed Taiwan today
without incident

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.667
after weeks of tension
with China over the visit.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.167
I mean,
that's playing with fire,

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:05.234
an 82-year-old getting on
a plane right now?

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.767
U.N. Secretary General
Antonio Guterres on Monday

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:12.701
said that humanity is, quote,

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:15.334
"one miscalculation away
from nuclear annihilation."

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:18.567
It was the worst
best man speech ever.

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:22.367
According to the latest numbers,
after Taco Bell bought --

00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:23.467
brought back, excuse me --

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.234
the Mexican pizza to its menu
in May,

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:27.367
demand was seven times higher

00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:29.467
than when the item
was previously available.

00:02:29.467 --> 00:02:32.701
Also seven times higher?
The people ordering them.

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:35.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:46.601
"Does that say Mexican pizza?"

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:49.567
And finally, New York's MTA
announced plans last week

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.100
to provide cellphone service

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.868
while traveling
between stations.

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:56.734
No word on whether they also
plan to offer train service.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:59.167
It will be helpful to have
the cellphone service.

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:01.100
No, it's not.
It's not here.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.534
That was a monologue,
everybody.

